# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Tutorial Hub
# Your starting point for learning JVN scripting.
# Each lesson is a separate .vns file you can open, edit, and break apart.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_hub
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1700]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.28]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.42]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]

Lavender: Hey there! I'm Lavender, your guide through these tutorials.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Everything here lives in {b}scripts/tutorial/{/b} — real {b}.vns{/b} files you can open side-by-side in the editor.
Lavender: Feel free to edit them, break things, add your own notes. That's the whole point.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: So — where do you want to start?

@label topics_page_1
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: These cover the bread and butter — dialogue, pacing, characters, and visuals.
> 01. Dialogue and Text Tags -> open_dialogue
> 02. Narration and Pacing -> open_narration
> 03. Expressions and Characters -> open_expressions
> 04. Images and Backgrounds -> open_images
> More topics -> topics_page_2
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_2
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Now for the fun stuff — effects, audio, branching logic, and animation tools.
> 05. Transitions and Screen FX -> open_transitions
> 06. Audio and Music -> open_audio
> 07. Variables and Conditions -> open_variables
> 08. Character Movement -> open_movement
> 09. Puppeteer Timelines -> open_puppeteer
> 10. Choices and Menus -> open_menus
> 11. Subroutines and Flow -> open_subroutines
> 12. Best Practices -> open_best_practices
> More topics -> topics_page_3
> Back to fundamentals -> topics_page_1
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_3
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Production-level topics — polish, localization, and shipping your game.
> 13. Camera and Staging -> open_camera
> 14. Localization -> open_localization
> 15. UI Layout and Themes -> open_ui_layout
> 16. Testing and Release -> open_testing_release
> Back to fundamentals -> topics_page_1
> Back to systems -> topics_page_2
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label open_dialogue
[goto {{DIALOGUE_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_narration
[goto {{NARRATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_expressions
[goto {{EXPRESSIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_images
[goto {{IMAGES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_transitions
[goto {{TRANSITIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_audio
[goto {{AUDIO_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_variables
[goto {{VARIABLES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_movement
[goto {{MOVEMENT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_puppeteer
[goto {{PUPPETEER_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_menus
[goto {{MENUS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_subroutines
[goto {{SUBROUTINES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_best_practices
[goto {{BEST_PRACTICES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_camera
[goto {{CAMERA_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_localization
[goto {{LOCALIZATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_ui_layout
[goto {{UI_LAYOUT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_testing_release
[goto {{TESTING_RELEASE_TARGET}}:start]

@label end_early
[show lavender center talking]
[wait 160]
[if tutorial_count > 13]
Lavender: You made it through almost everything — nice stamina!
[elif tutorial_count > 7]
Lavender: Solid run. You've got a good foundation to build on.
[elif tutorial_count > 2]
Lavender: Good start! The rest will be here whenever you need them.
[else]
Lavender: No rush — pick up wherever you left off next time.
[endif]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Remember, these files are yours. Annotate them, remix them, make them part of your project.
Lavender: Happy writing!
[end]
